# CQ-P07: Does every tenant keep at least one admin who is not removed?
# A constraint: each row is a tenant that keeps none, so the answer is yes when no row comes back, read beside the
# companion that finds the tenants that do keep one. It starts from each tenant, never from the memberships, so a
# tenant with no members is a row (report 04 section 3.1). An admin who is not removed is a member whose stage is
# active, holding a grant of the admin role (decision 136); the grant's scope is not read (report 18 section 10).
# Each type step walks down the subclasses (decision 27), so a node typed by a subclass is found too.
PREFIX inv: <https://example.org/inventory-import/ontology/>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?tenant
WHERE {
  ?tenant rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* inv:Tenant .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?member rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* inv:Member ;
            inv:membershipIn ?tenant ;
            inv:membershipStatus inv:MembershipStatusScheme-active .
    ?grant rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* inv:Grant ;
           inv:grantedTo ?member ;
           inv:grantsRole inv:MemberRoleScheme-admin .
  }
}
ORDER BY ?tenant
